is (ALS)\n\nWhere 1\n\n  * Worldwide Clinical Trials\n\nSan Antonio, Texas, United States--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nORT247 in Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis (ALS) - Clinical Trials Registry - ICH GCP (https://ichgcp.net/amp/clinical-trials-registry/NCT06769620)\nciteturn666search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; Crawled: last month; January 13, 2025 updated by: Orthogonal Neuroscience Inc. ...   * Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis (ALS) ...   * Known history of hypersensitivity to any component of the ORT247 drug product or placebo\n\n# A First in Human Study of ORT247 in Healthy Volunteers\n\nJanuary 13, 2025 updated by: Orthogonal Neuroscience Inc.\n\n## A Phase 1, Randomized, Double-blind, Placebo-Controlled, Single-Ascending-Dose Study to Evaluate the Safety, Tolerability, Immunogenicity, and Pharmacokinetics of Intravenous ORT247 in Healthy Volunteers\n\nThis is a single center, double-blinded, randomized, placebo controlled single ascending dose clinical study, with the primary purpose of evaluating the safety, tolerability, pharmacokinetics (PK), and immunohistochemistry of escalating intravenous doses of ORT247 in healthy volunteers.\n\n## Study Overview\n\n#### Status\n\n## Status\n\nIndicates the current recruitment status or the expanded access status.\n\nCompleted\n\n#### Conditions\n\n## Conditions\n\nThe disease, disorder, syndrome, illness, or injury that is being studied. On ClinicalTrials.gov, conditions may also include other health-related issues, such as lifespan, quality of life, and health risks.\n\n  * Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis (ALS)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPNS 2022 Abstract Supplement (https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1111/jns.12506)\nciteturn666search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.4 years ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; ## DEVELOPMENT OF ORT247, A MONOCLONAL ANTIBODY ANTAGONIST OF EPHA4, FOR THE TREATMENT OF CMT AND ALS\nAn extensive nonclinical program was conducted to evaluate the safety and efficacy of ORT247 in preparation for possible human clinical trials in CMT and ALS.\n\nMethods: The affinity and selectivity of ORT247 for EphA4 were evaluated by SPR and ELISA assays. Functional activity was demonstrated in cultured neurons. In vivo efficacy studies were conducted in mouse models of ALS and of CMT1a and CMT2e. Safety studies were conducted in mouse and non-human primate.\n\nResults: ORT247 binds with high affinity to the ligand-binding domain of EphA4 and exhibits 10–100-fold selectivity for EphA4 compared with other EphA/EphB receptors. ORT247 blocks ligand-induced EphA4 clustering, downstream signaling, and axon growth cone collapse in cultured cortical neurons. In vivo studies show that ORT247 treatment enhances NMJ innervation, promotes nerve conduction, decreases serum neurofilament levels, and improves functional outcomes, such as muscle strength and locomotor deficits, in the transgenic mouse models of Charcot–Marie–Tooth type 1a and 2e. Additionally, ORT247 improves NMJ function as measured electrophysiologically in SOD1 G93A mice. The safety of ORT247 is supported by toxicology studies conducted in CD-1 mice and cynomolgus monkeys administered ORT247 via intraperitoneal injection and intravenous infusion, respectively.\n\nConclusions: Nonclinical efficacy and safety data support the clinical development of ORT247 in patients with CMT and ALS.\n\nKeywords: EphA4 receptor, ephrin, neuromuscular junction, CMT1a, CMT2e\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDDrare: Database of Drug Development for Rare Diseases (https://ddrare.nibn.go.jp/cgi-bin/disease_info.cgi?id=2&tab=ds)\nciteturn666search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; ORT247 ...       2022   Phase 1   NCT06769620   United States\nOther: symptomatic treatment OF ALS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPNS